eminders, reflections of inner power and divine essence. Each piece acts as an echo of what already lives within you, supporting empowerment, grounding, and remembrance through intentional adornment and high-vibrational design.<\/p><p>We believe that how you dress your body is how you dress your spirit. Every talisman we craft carries intention—not trend, not trend-chasing perfection, but presence. Our pieces are made slowly, by hand, to honor both the wearer and the work. We create for women who understand that jewelry is ceremony, that symbols are teachers, and that beauty rooted in meaning lasts longer than anything shiny.<\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"narrow","alignment":"left","type_preset":"custom","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"1.125rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground-heading)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}}},"block_order":["text_VKVrw3","text_36UQ6L"]},"image_ET3pbN":{"type":"image","settings":{"image":"shopify:\/\/shop_images\/IMG_7270.jpg","link":"","image_ratio":"adapt","width":"fill","custom_width":100,"width_mobile":"fill","custom_width_mobile":100,"height":"fit","border":"none","border_width":1,"border_opacity":100,"border_radius":40,"padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":76,"padding-inline-end":76},"blocks":{}},"group_GdhRgE":{"type":"group","settings":{"content_direction":"column","vertical_on_mobile":true,"horizontal_alignment":"flex-start","vertical_alignment":"center","align_baseline":false,"horizontal_alignment_flex_direction_column":"flex-start","vertical_alignment_flex_direction_column":"center","gap":12,"width":"custom","custom_width":100,"width_mobile":"fill","custom_width_mobile":100,"height":"fit","custom_height":100,"inherit_color_scheme":true,"color_scheme":"","background_media":"none","video_position":"cover","background_image_position":"cover","border":"none","border_width":1,"border_opacity":100,"border_radius":0,"toggle_overlay":false,"overlay_color":"#00000026","overlay_style":"solid","gradient_direction":"to top","link":"","open_in_new_tab":false,"placeholder":"","padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{"text_RaHdwK":{"type":"text","name":"t:names.heading","settings":{"text":"<p>Who We Are<\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"normal","alignment":"left","type_preset":"h2","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"1rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground-heading)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}},"text_VdFNA6":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>Chandrāma Ritual is an intentional jewelry brand creating pieces rooted in ancient symbols, sacred geometry, and ancestral adornment. Each creation is designed with care and presence, meant to be worn as protection, grounding, and remembrance. These are not decorative objects, but daily companions—supporting inner strength, awareness, and a deeper connection to self.<\/p><p>We are makers, not manufacturers. Every chain is tied by hand. Every stone is placed with intention. Every symbol is chosen because it carries weight, literal and spiritual. We work with brass, quartz, natural stones, and materials that feel alive against skin. Our designs honor lunar cycles, divine feminine power, and the quiet magic that lives in slowness. We create for the woman who dresses like a ritual, who trusts her intuition, and who knows that what she wears shapes how she moves through the world.<\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"narrow","alignment":"left","type_preset":"custom","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"1.125rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground-heading)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}}},"block_order":["text_RaHdwK","text_VdFNA6"]}},"block_order":["group_qaKiEp","image_ET3pbN","group_GdhRgE"],"name":"t:names.image_with_text","settings":{"content_direction":"row","vertical_on_mobile":true,"horizontal_alignment":"flex-start","vertical_alignment":"center","align_baseline":false,"horizontal_alignment_flex_direction_column":"flex-start","vertical_alignment_flex_direction_column":"center","gap":32,"section_width":"page-width","section_height":"","section_height_custom":50,"color_scheme":"","background_media":"none","video_position":"cover","background_image_position":"cover","border":"none","border_width":1,"border_opacity":100,"border_radius":0,"toggle_overlay":false,"overlay_color":"#00000026","overlay_style":"solid","gradient_direction":"to top","padding-block-start":40,"padding-block-end":40}},"section_iMFCLD":{"type":"section","blocks":{"group_yQ7Gib":{"type":"group","settings":{"content_direction":"column","vertical_on_mobile":true,"horizontal_alignment":"flex-start","vertical_alignment":"center","align_baseline":false,"horizontal_alignment_flex_direction_column":"flex-start","vertical_alignment_flex_direction_column":"center","gap":12,"width":"custom","custom_width":100,"width_mobile":"fill","custom_width_mobile":100,"height":"fit","custom_height":100,"inherit_color_scheme":true,"color_scheme":"","background_media":"none","video_position":"cover","background_image_position":"cover","border":"none","border_width":1,"border_opacity":100,"border_radius":0,"toggle_overlay":false,"overlay_color":"#00000026","overlay_style":"solid","gradient_direction":"to top","link":"","open_in_new_tab":false,"placeholder":"","padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{"text_C9WcMG":{"type":"text","name":"t:names.heading","settings":{"text":"<p>Founder Story<\/p>","width":"100%","max_width":"normal","alignment":"left","type_preset":"h2","font":"var(--font-body--family)","font_size":"1rem","line_height":"normal","letter_spacing":"normal","case":"none","wrap":"pretty","color":"var(--color-foreground-heading)","background":false,"background_color":"#00000026","corner_radius":0,"padding-block-start":0,"padding-block-end":0,"padding-inline-start":0,"padding-inline-end":0},"blocks":{}},"text_pqngQn":{"type":"text","settings":{"text":"<p>Chandrāma Ritual was born from a quiet realization: that jewelry could be more than decoration. Wearing my first self-made talisman changed something—I felt more present, more anchored, more at home within myself. I discovered how deeply nourishing the process of making slowly, with intention, with my hands, truly was. During that time, I began learning about lunar cycles, sacred geometry, and wrist adornment across cultures—where it has long been worn as a symbol of protection, grounding, and feminine power. I searched for something that carried that depth of meaning, but couldn't find what I was looking for. So, eventually, I made one for myself.<\/p><p>Art has always been part of my life, but at a certain point, I felt a deep pull to create with my hands in a way that felt devotional. That desire arrived at the same time I was feeling disconnected from my femininity, disempowered, and longing to reconnect with my own inner strength. Creating became my ritual. I began Chandrāma Ritual because I was searching for jewelry that could remind me—and others—that we are sacred, powerful, and woven into something greater. I wanted pieces that felt like mirrors and talismans, not accessories. Objects that could hold meaning, awaken something within, and be worn as a form of devotion. Pieces for women who dress like a ceremony.<\/p>","width":"100%